# Step-Keys: Delivery Workflow Dictionary

Spec: StepKeys
Purpose:
  Canonical dictionary of the 24 short keys used by the delivery workflow
  (chain DL1). Keys are CANONICAL — they are never redefined during
  execution. Every key maps to an SDD stage (workflow/stages.sdd) or a
  scoped instance of one.

Owns: workflow/step-keys.sdd

Source: user-provided WORKFLOW AGENT core rules, integrated Phase 151
(2026-09-11) after gap analysis vs existing stage registry.

Dictionary:
  BC    Business Case
        Purpose: Understand the business problem, goal, scope and context.
        Stage: BC (business stages group)
  BR    Business Requirement
        Purpose: Define what the business requires from the system.
        Stage: BR
  BD    Business Design
        Purpose: Define the business-level solution/design.
        Stage: BD
  DS    Decision
        Purpose: Record and finalize important decisions derived from
                 requirements/design.
        Stage: DS (decision-ledger write step)
  TK    Task
        Purpose: Break the approved work into actionable technical tasks.
        Stage: TK (task engine step)
  BDD   Behavior-Driven Development
        Purpose: Define expected behavior/scenarios before implementation.
        Stage: BDD
  BE    Backend
        Purpose: Implement backend/business logic.
        Stage: BE
  CR-BE Code Review — Backend
        Purpose: Review backend implementation against requirements,
                 design and BDD.
        Stage: CR instance scoped to BE (see CRScopedSemantics)
  RF-BE Refactor — Backend
        Purpose: Address CR-BE findings; restructure/clean backend code
                 before security validation.
        Stage: RF instance scoped to BE
  SC-BE Security — Backend
        Purpose: Scoped security validation BEFORE branch tests
                 (v2 ordering, Phase 155).
        Stage: SC instance scoped to BE
  BE-TS Backend Tests
        Purpose: Test and validate Backend behavior AFTER the scoped
                 security pass (SC-BE).
        Stage: BE_TS
  DB    Database
        Purpose: Design/implement database structure, schema, migrations.
        Stage: DB
  CR-DB Code Review — Database
        Purpose: Review database changes and consistency.
        Stage: CR instance scoped to DB
  RF-DB Refactor — Database
        Purpose: Address CR-DB findings; restructure/clean database 
                 schema/migrations before security validation.
        Stage: RF instance scoped to DB
  SC-DB Security — Database
        Purpose: Scoped security validation BEFORE branch tests
                 (v2 ordering, Phase 155).
        Stage: SC instance scoped to DB
  DB-TS Database Tests
        Purpose: Test and validate Database behavior AFTER the scoped
                 security pass (SC-DB).
        Stage: DB_TS
  API   API Development
        Purpose: Implement API endpoints/contracts/integration.
        Stage: API
  CR-API Code Review — API
        Purpose: Review API implementation and contracts.
        Stage: CR instance scoped to API
  RF-API Refactor — API
        Purpose: Address CR-API findings; restructure/clean API
                 implementation and contracts before security validation.
        Stage: RF instance scoped to API
  SC-API Security — API
        Purpose: Scoped security validation BEFORE branch tests
                 (v2 ordering, Phase 155).
        Stage: SC instance scoped to API
  API-TS API Tests
        Purpose: Test and validate API behavior and contracts AFTER
                 the scoped security pass (SC-API).
        Stage: BE_TS scoped to API contracts
  FE    Frontend
        Purpose: Implement web/frontend functionality.
        Stage: FE
  CR-FE Code Review — Frontend
        Purpose: Review frontend implementation.
        Stage: CR instance scoped to FE
  RF-FE Refactor — Frontend
        Purpose: Address CR-FE findings; restructure/clean frontend
                 implementation before security validation.
        Stage: RF instance scoped to FE
  SC-FE Security — Frontend
        Purpose: Scoped security validation BEFORE branch tests
                 (v2 ordering, Phase 155).
        Stage: SC instance scoped to FE
  FE-TS Frontend Tests
        Purpose: Test and validate frontend behavior AFTER the scoped
                 security pass (SC-FE).
        Stage: FE_TS
  MD    Mobile Development
        Purpose: Implement mobile application functionality.
        Stage: MD
  CR-MD Code Review — Mobile
        Purpose: Review mobile implementation.
        Stage: CR instance scoped to MD
  RF-MD Refactor — Mobile
        Purpose: Address CR-MD findings; restructure/clean mobile
                 implementation before security validation.
        Stage: RF instance scoped to MD
  SC-MD Security — Mobile
        Purpose: Scoped security validation BEFORE branch tests
                 (v2 ordering, Phase 155).
        Stage: SC instance scoped to MD
  MD-TS Mobile Development Tests
        Purpose: Test and validate mobile functionality AFTER the
                 scoped security pass (SC-MD).
        Stage: MD_TS
  DC    Documentation
        Purpose: Create/update technical and project documentation.
        Stage: DC
  CR-DC Code Review — Documentation
        Purpose: Review documentation for correctness and consistency.
        Stage: CR instance scoped to DC
  RF-DC Refactor — Documentation
        Purpose: Address CR-DC findings; restructure/clean documentation
                 for correctness and consistency before security validation.
        Stage: RF instance scoped to DC
  SC-DC Security — Documentation
        Purpose: Scoped security validation BEFORE branch validation
                 (v2 ordering, Phase 155) — no secrets/credentials in
                 docs, no sensitive data exposure.
        Stage: SC instance scoped to DC
  DC-TS Documentation Tests / Validation
        Purpose: Validate documentation against the actual
                 implementation AFTER the scoped security pass (SC-DC).
        Stage: DC-TS
  FTS   Final Test Suite
        Purpose: Cross-layer E2E, integration, and regression over all
                 ACTIVE branches after their XX-TS complete; closes the
                 layer loop before AN ([DL1-8]).
        Stage: TS scoped to cross-layer (see FTSScopedSemantics)
  AN    Analysis
        Purpose: Analyze the complete workflow state and cross-check all
                 outputs.
        Stage: AN
  VR    Verification
        Purpose: Final verification of the complete workflow.
        Stage: VR

Mapping (key -> existing SDD stage):
  BC -> BC (new stage, stages.sdd business group)
  BR -> BR (new stage)
  BD -> BD (new stage)
  DS -> DS (new stage; runtime = decision ledger DEC-XXX records)
  TK -> TK (new stage; runtime = tasks/INDEX.sdd entries)
  BDD -> BDD (existing)
  BE -> BE (existing)
  CR-BE -> CR { scope: BE }
  RF-BE -> RF { scope: BE }
  SC-BE -> SC { scope: BE }
  BE-TS -> BE_TS (existing)
  DB -> DB (existing)
  CR-DB -> CR { scope: DB }
  RF-DB -> RF { scope: DB }
  SC-DB -> SC { scope: DB }
  DB-TS -> DB_TS (existing)
  API -> API (existing)
  CR-API -> CR { scope: API }
  RF-API -> RF { scope: API }
  SC-API -> SC { scope: API }
  API-TS -> BE_TS { scope: API contracts }
  FE -> FE (existing)
  CR-FE -> CR { scope: FE }
  RF-FE -> RF { scope: FE }
  SC-FE -> SC { scope: FE }
  FE-TS -> FE_TS (existing)
  MD -> MD (existing)
  CR-MD -> CR { scope: MD }
  RF-MD -> RF { scope: MD }
  SC-MD -> SC { scope: MD }
  MD-TS -> MD_TS (existing)
  DC -> DC (new stage)
  CR-DC -> CR { scope: DC }
  RF-DC -> RF { scope: DC }
  SC-DC -> SC { scope: DC }
  DC-TS -> DC_TS (new stage)
  FTS -> TS { scope: cross-layer }
  AN -> AN (existing)
  VR -> VR (existing)

CRScopedSemantics:
  definition: CR is ONE stage (peer review before merge). CR-XX keys are
    the SAME stage executed with a `scope:` parameter naming the branch
    artifact under review (BE, DB, API, FE, MD, DC).
  rule: scoped instances are NOT new stages — no stage explosion; each
    CR-XX execution reviews that branch's output against its requirements,
    design and BDD.
  rule: a branch is complete only when its CR-XX has passed.
  rule: CR-XX includes the dependency diff check — any undeclared new
    dependency found in the diff fails the review (bax
    ../gates/dependency-gate.sdd).

RFScopedSemantics:
  definition: RF is ONE stage (post-review refactor) executed with a
    `scope:` parameter naming the branch artifact (BE, DB, API, FE, MD, DC).
  rule: RF-XX keys are NOT new stages — same RF stage, scoped instance.
  rule: RF-XX runs only after its CR-XX has passed with change requests,
        or is skipped if CR-XX passes clean.
  rule: XX-TS validates the branch only after RF-XX (if triggered) is
        done AND after its SC-XX has passed (v2 ordering).

SCScopedSemantics:
  definition: SC is ONE stage (security validation). SC-XX keys are the
    SAME stage executed with a `scope:` parameter naming the branch
    artifact (BE, DB, API, FE, MD, DC).
  rule: SC-XX keys are NOT new stages — same SC stage, scoped instance.
  rule: SC-XX runs after RF-XX (or CR-XX directly when RF-XX was
        skipped) and BEFORE XX-TS (v2 ordering, Phase 155).
  rule: a branch's XX-TS is reachable only after its SC-XX passed —
        security-defective code is never tested first.

FTSScopedSemantics:
  definition: FTS is a TS stage instance scoped to cross-layer: E2E,
    integration, and regression across all ACTIVE branches.
  rule: FTS depends on every active branch's XX-TS; skipped branches
        (outside ImpactMatrix) are excluded from FTS scope.
  rule: FTS is mandatory per [DL1-8]; explicit StageSkip with recorded
        reason is the only skip path.

Concepts:
  Layer:   A branch DOMAIN of the delivery chain — BE, DB, API, FE,
           MD, DC (bax ../chains/delivery.sdd). Layers are where
           implementation happens.
  Gate:    A mandatory quality TRANSITION — CR (peer review), RF
           (post-review refactor), SC (security validation), TS
           (tests/validation). Gates are scoped per layer (CR-XX) but
           are never layers themselves.
  Stage:   A named engineering responsibility with inputs/outputs/gate
           criteria (bax ../workflow/stages.sdd) — Layers and Gates
           both resolve to stage instances.
  Ordering: v2 (Phase 155) — within each branch: XX -> CR-XX -> RF-XX ->
           SC-XX -> XX-TS; FTS after all branches; keys unchanged [SK1].

Rules:
  [SK1] Short keys are CANONICAL — never redefined during execution.
  [SK2] Every key resolves through this dictionary — no improvised meanings.
  [SK3] CR-XX keys are scoped CR instances (scope parameter), not stages.
  [SK4] API-TS maps to BE_TS scoped to API contracts (API testing lives in
        the backend test suite discipline).
  [SK5] The dictionary is the ONLY place keys are defined; execution
        references keys, never invents new ones.
  [SK6] Within-branch ordering is v2: SC-XX precedes XX-TS — a branch's
        tests never run before its security pass (Phase 155).

Navigation:
  Stages: @stages.sdd
  Transitions: @transitions.sdd
  DeliveryChain: @../chains/delivery.sdd
  WorkflowIndex: @INDEX.sdd
  TaskStateMachine: @../tasks/TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd

